WEBVTT

00:01:57.230 --> 00:02:00.000
I can't hear you.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.070
The president, the first vice president, the second vice president.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:15.950
You got an appointment?

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.120
For seven years.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:24.450
Baby, I can help you.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.000
Welcome home.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.760
welcome home good to see you max boy we sure missed you it's about time come on let's sit

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:10.240
down we got left to talk about sit right here max how about some wine max good we'll all have

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:19.510
some here yeah absolutely you look great max never looked better did he tell yeah he's even

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:25.560
got a good tan just in time for lunch we'll go to luigi's nice thick steaks food can win

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.440
remember luigi's max taste that the best

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:31.920
- First thing you need is some new clothes.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.100
Have I got a tailor, uptown, shoulders?

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.230
- When Max wants clothes, he'll buy clothes.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:39.510
When he wants to eat, he'll eat.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.930
Maybe there's other things he wants first.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:44.880
Max knows what he wants, didn't he always?

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:45.920
And it all costs money.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:48.540
Everything costs money, huh, Max?

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:51.530
Here's $1,000.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:52.530
- I notice you got the painting

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.110
of Pa hanging downstairs.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:56.340
- It's a copy of the one at the house.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.390
- It's a nice touch.

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:00.000
Banks should always hang paintings of the dead

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.660
It gives them a sense of tradition, like this one.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.700
This bank stinks with tradition.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:08.920
- Max, Pa's been dead five years. Let it rest. - Take the money, Max.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.470
Where's Ma living? I called the house. There was no answer.

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:18.270
- But what's wrong? - Nothing.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:23.710
- Doesn't she live at the big house anymore? - But she moved.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.200
- Where? - Back on Mulberry Street.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:30.000
- Why? - Well, who knows? We kept the big house at home.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.850
Just as it was, she won't go near it.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:34.800
Come on, drink up, we've got a whole bottle to kill.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:42.280
I kind of lost my taste for champagne.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:45.250
Cigars, too.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:53.370
Big, rich bank.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.710
Must be quite a responsibility.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:58.840
Lots of big, rich worries.

00:05:58.840 --> 00:05:59.830
You know something, Joe?

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.810
You look worried.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:05.840
Me? I've got nothing to worry about. I got nothing. Period.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:10.800
- How's Maria? - Fine.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:14.350
- Is she still as beautiful? - Yeah.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.640
You know, being married has got its worries too.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.630
Especially to a beautiful girl like Maria.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:23.390
Does she ever ask about me?

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:26.080
- I must come up to dinner soon. - Anytime, Max.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.580
It's a nice family you got, Joe.

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:34.930
Two kids.

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:36.810
Blondes like their mother.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:41.590
How good time has been to you.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:43.150
To all three of you.

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:47.710
Tony's got Maria.

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:50.300
Two blonde kids who hate spaghetti.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:51.640
Pietro.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:53.030
Second vice president.

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:57.110
I can remember when your greatest ambition was 50 bucks for six rounds.

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:00.000
Yes, time has been.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.710
but tell me, why do you all look so worried?

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:06.990
- What do you want, Max? - Seven years. I want them back.

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:08.970
- How much? - I told you.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:11.070
It's not working, Max. You're not scaring anyone.

00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:17.020
I want seven years back. I see you, brothers.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:20.040
Better take the money. It's all you get.

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:34.250
- Buster's head. - He's out for blood.

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:37.140
You'll get blood. Plenty of blood.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.390
- Who you calling? - Angelino.

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:41.380
We don't need Angelino.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:44.880
We're gonna keep it in the family where it belongs.

00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:47.160
It's always been.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:54.900
A man who throws away money is a big worry.

00:07:55.820 --> 00:08:00.000
Big problem.

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:29.080
- Saturday night. How come you're home on a Saturday night? - You don't ask girls questions like that?

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:32.720
If you must know, nobody asked me.

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:34.590
There always was your trouble.

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:35.670
Unpopular.

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:37.210
I guess you've been alone every night.

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:38.970
Nobody's that unpopular.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:40.870
Who?

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:43.080
Anyone to kill time with.

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:44.380
You've had a lot of time to kill.

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:46.280
A lot of time killers.

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:49.800
Have you seen your brothers?

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:52.110
I had to see them before anything.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:52.880
And?

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:58.970
Don't be like that, Max.

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:00.000
Especially not tonight.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.560
How did you expect me to be? Full of jokes? Happy Max, laughing boy?

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:06.560
It's over. Seven years past and gone. Forget them.

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:12.030
Vengeance is a rare wine. A joy divine, says the Arab. I'm gonna get drunk on it.

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:16.180
What did you pick that up? Some philosopher in the death house?

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:18.100
Then you've come back a fool.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:21.470
Check. I was once the smartest of them all. What did it get me?

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:26.270
Us. You and me and everything we've waited for.

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:30.000
Max, let's get out of New York tonight. Let's go to San Francisco.

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:32.210
You can start again, whatever you want.

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:34.300
What I want is right here in New York.

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:36.300
Just what goes on in that fine Italian brain of yours?

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:40.560
Murder? Is that what you planned for seven years? A vendetta?

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:42.060
That's how I killed time.

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:43.060
What about me?

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:45.060
I was in a jail for seven years.

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:46.950
I was in a bigger jail than yours.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:48.950
I was in a jailer sight of the world.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:50.970
You'll have to wait a little longer.

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:55.620
I've done my last night's waiting.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:13:00.000
Let me have the porter, please.

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:02.450
- I'm getting two tickets on a plane to San Francisco.

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:03.650
- You'll have one empty seat.

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:06.700
- It's now or never.

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:09.630
- You mustn't threaten an Italian.

00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:13.350
It doesn't mix well in our blood.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:15.520
- Am I part of your vendetta?

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:17.360
Am I on your list?

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:19.960
Isn't it enough to destroy your brothers and yourself?

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:21.310
Why me?

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:23.200
Why did you come back to me at all?

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:24.480
And for what?

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:27.680
A dead man, an evil man, a bad man.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.000
You're filled with this poison, it breathes in you.

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:33.340
The world's better off with your father dead, but you're not.

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:36.430
Good boy.

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:38.430
That's what Gino Manetti likes.

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:40.210
It's the truth because it hurts.

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:41.710
Hate, Max. Hate.

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:42.910
Don't ever love.

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:44.660
Listen to your dead father.

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:30.610
Hmm.

00:16:45.960 --> 00:17:00.000
The nine power. We've got to get to that.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.620
- The bank will open it when I get there. - The depositors will be waiting.

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:07.590
Who else will pay my kind of interest? For my kind of interest, I can wait.

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:15.080
Here, scrub on my back.

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:20.850
Higher, higher, higher.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:24.450
Oh, that's good. A little load now.

00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:28.990
A little load. Harder, harder.

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:33.940
I've got a scrub, a scrub a heart.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:44.290
- Buongiorno, Signor Monero.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:51.800
- Buongiorno, Signor Monero.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:58.320
- Buongiorno.

00:17:58.320 --> 00:17:59.640
- Where are you, Signor?

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:01.920
You're looking at me.

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:46.080
The import people are calling again about their loan.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:48.050
Now the shipment is on the dock.

00:18:48.050 --> 00:18:49.450
Not now, after a little while.

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:51.360
First, I take care of my friends.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:52.960
Oh, look up.

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:58.980
Parla, parla, inglesse, qui siamo in America.

00:18:58.980 --> 00:19:00.000
How many time I tell you?

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.420
English. You gotta learn some time.

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:04.260
I'm gonna need some money

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:05.380
to buy one horse.

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:06.900
What for you need a horse?

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:09.750
The old one, she die. She cannot pick up junk.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:11.740
How much it cost one horse?

00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:13.850
One hundred and fifty dollars.

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:23.450
Oh, fifty. All right, sign here, Luca.

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:28.260
You okay eighty thousand dollars

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:29.060
on the housing project?

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:29.960
Si.

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:32.920
The fellow from Chicago's on the telephone.

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:34.800
Wants to know if you renew on the brewery.

00:19:35.510 --> 00:19:37.810
- Hello? - Gino Manetti.

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:41.680
- No. - Yes.

00:19:52.110 --> 00:19:54.740
But, Gino, this is only $120.

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:59.830
Interest. I take him out in advance.

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:17.760
You better send them to Denver.

00:20:17.760 --> 00:20:23.370
That's a long trip. That's in Kansas.

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:28.090
- How much? - The train cost 62 dollars.

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:30.000
Hey, Donny!

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:34.960
You know what is the banking hours?

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:36.250
Nine to three, Pa.

00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:37.790
But you never open on time.

00:20:37.870 --> 00:20:40.010
Whenever you mind when I open, you open on time.

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:41.480
What's the matter of your nose?

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:43.020
I won last night.

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:44.540
By a knockout in the second round.

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:45.360
How would you get?

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:46.910
I can't take money.

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:48.470
It would hurt my amateur standing.

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:49.580
No money?

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:50.750
Then why you fight?

00:20:51.190 --> 00:20:52.310
It's sport, Pa.

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:53.480
You fight too?

00:20:53.910 --> 00:20:54.590
I'm his manager.

00:20:54.990 --> 00:20:56.150
He's also a sport, huh?

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:57.970
Go on, go to work.

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:00.000
Do sports, son.

00:21:00.250 --> 00:21:09.360
Oh, sorry, I make a mistake.

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:15.960
No, no, no, no. Bye, bye, my dear, my dear. Bye, bye.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:23.200
Will you come here a minute? I want to show you something.

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:34.360
You've got to make Max get an office somewhere else.

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:36.340
Look at those characters hanging around.

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:37.740
They're getting worse and worse all the time.

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:39.060
They give the bank a black eye.

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:40.520
Well, Max, he'd bring good business.

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:41.960
Bail bonds for criminals.

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:43.700
After all, we're running a bank park.

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:44.900
What do you mean, a we?

00:21:45.310 --> 00:21:46.550
I am the bank.

00:21:47.220 --> 00:21:48.420
Go on, go back to your cage.

00:21:58.710 --> 00:21:59.030
Momento.

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:00.000
No free.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:03.700
- You want to fill the fountain pen, you go to the post office. - Post office.

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:13.460
- Hello, Petro. - Yeah, Pa.

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:16.450
- Go see what the lady wants. - Yeah, Pa.

00:22:16.680 --> 00:22:20.590
- Yes, ma'am. - Where will I find Mr. Minetti?

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:23.590
We got lots of Minetti's here. My father, my brother Joe, Tony...

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:27.760
- Which one is the attorney? - Oh, the lawyer. Max.

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:29.760
Thank you.

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:34.910
I sent him a gun.

00:22:38.270 --> 00:22:39.150
Oh, Al, you all right?

00:22:39.150 --> 00:22:41.150
Yes, go ahead. You told me that. Did he have a gun?

00:22:41.150 --> 00:22:42.710
That's bad.

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:43.710
Any witnesses?

00:22:43.710 --> 00:22:45.170
Very bad.

00:22:45.170 --> 00:22:46.650
Has he got any money?

00:22:46.650 --> 00:22:48.460
Good.

00:22:48.460 --> 00:22:56.110
Yeah.

00:22:56.110 --> 00:22:57.110
Doors are made to knock on.

00:22:57.110 --> 00:22:58.060
I haven't got time.

00:22:58.060 --> 00:23:00.000
Whoever it is, say you'll call them out.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:03.830
No, I'll call you back.

00:23:03.830 --> 00:23:09.580
- Where do your clients sit? - They don't, period.

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:12.190
My name is Irene Bennett.

00:23:12.190 --> 00:23:13.170
What's your story?

00:23:13.170 --> 00:23:16.510
You were recommended to me by the firm of Hanford, Sloan & Elliott.

00:23:16.510 --> 00:23:19.010
Oh, it's a very high-class firm. I used to work for them.

00:23:19.010 --> 00:23:21.040
They don't recommend many clients to me unless...

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:23.540
- Unless what? - Unless they're low-class.

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:27.560
A friend of mine is in trouble with the police.

00:23:27.560 --> 00:23:29.880
- What did he do? - What makes you say he?

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:33.330
You don't look like you go to all this trouble for a woman, so what did he do?

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:38.050
Oh, a lot of things. Bad checks, took some jewelry, sold someone else's car.

00:23:38.150 --> 00:23:41.170
- What's he to you? - I said he was a friend.

00:23:41.330 --> 00:23:46.110
- Hmm. This car and jewelry, yours, weren't they? - Yes.

00:23:46.210 --> 00:23:49.490
So what you got to worry about are the bad checks. Why don't you make them good?

00:23:49.880 --> 00:23:52.910
It's too late. They were turned over to the district attorney.

00:23:52.920 --> 00:23:54.000
What do you want me to do?

00:23:54.600 --> 00:23:58.580
I'll give you my check to cover them in your fees. That should clean things up.

00:23:58.580 --> 00:24:00.000
Money is a great claim.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.100
He was worth it.

00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:04.200
Maybe to you, but not to me.

00:24:04.200 --> 00:24:05.200
What's wrong?

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:09.520
I'm a lawyer, not a garbage man.

00:24:09.520 --> 00:24:12.860
You think he can skip through life with a checkbook.

00:24:12.860 --> 00:24:13.860
Opens and closes all the doors.

00:24:13.860 --> 00:24:14.860
I'm not that hard up.

00:24:14.860 --> 00:24:16.880
Take your business someplace else, period.

00:24:16.880 --> 00:24:18.990
That was a pretty insulting little speech.

00:24:18.990 --> 00:24:19.990
That's what I had in mind.

00:24:19.990 --> 00:24:20.990
But it didn't take.

00:24:20.990 --> 00:24:22.160
You can't insult women.

00:24:22.160 --> 00:24:23.190
You're not the type.

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:24.190
No?

00:24:24.190 --> 00:24:25.140
No.

00:24:25.140 --> 00:24:26.140
From you, they love it.

00:24:26.140 --> 00:24:27.920
Nothing touches you.

00:24:27.920 --> 00:24:29.930
Everything bounces off that chromium.

00:24:30.160 --> 00:24:32.770
The chromium's wearing thin.

00:24:32.770 --> 00:24:35.090
Look, I'm tired and I'm bored with this mess.

00:24:35.090 --> 00:24:36.230
Will you take my case?

00:24:36.230 --> 00:24:38.000
After what I said?

00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:40.750
Especially after what you said.

00:24:40.750 --> 00:24:43.810
Say please.

00:24:43.810 --> 00:24:44.890
I'll pay my way, thanks.

00:24:44.890 --> 00:24:45.890
Say please.

00:24:45.890 --> 00:24:46.840
Please.

00:24:46.840 --> 00:24:52.300
All right.

00:24:52.300 --> 00:24:57.890
I'll take your case, Miss, uh, Bennett.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:29.800
very good at remembering names. You'll remember my name? You busy? Come on in. Smell the air in here. Perfume? They sell it a drop at a time. You gotta have a doctor's prescription. Like chloroform, it gets in your brain.

00:25:30.280 --> 00:25:32.200
- Who was it? - A dame.

00:25:32.200 --> 00:25:35.160
- How's things at home? How's Elaine? - Okay.

00:25:35.160 --> 00:25:41.880
- What's on your mind? - You remember Pa promised to raise my salary after I was married.

00:25:41.880 --> 00:25:44.910
- Hasn't he done it? - No.

00:25:44.910 --> 00:25:48.710
Elaine's getting pretty sore. She says she thought she married a banker.

00:25:48.710 --> 00:25:53.490
Some banker. How can I entertain on $65 a week?

00:25:53.490 --> 00:25:56.820
- You've married her. Do you have to entertain her? - Her friends.

00:25:56.820 --> 00:25:59.280
After all, she comes from a fine Philadelphia family.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:05.170
social. Take her downtown, buy her a new dress, charge her to me. No, no, no. That won't do any

00:26:05.170 --> 00:26:11.350
good. Elaine's proud. First time she came into the bank and saw me behind the cage like a common

00:26:11.350 --> 00:26:15.490
clerk, she almost cried. She's sensitive. You mean she's impatient? Slow her down, Joe. You're

00:26:15.490 --> 00:26:19.880
