And if anything goes wrong?

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:41.040
even enough man to say what do you mean you're just in time huh did you know you brought up a

01:05:41.040 --> 01:05:54.600
house full of strangers strangers who do you think i build at the bank huh who do you think

01:05:54.600 --> 01:06:00.000
i work in a build building a work for me for mama we cannot live long enough to spend what we

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:05.690
got a long time ago. Mama wanted me to stop but no. I work in a build. I build in a worker.

01:06:05.690 --> 01:06:12.440
For what then? For my sons. For you, Joe. He's good I pay you a little. Then you know

01:06:12.440 --> 01:06:16.580
what it is to be poor. You remember when you're rich. It was right to pay you a little money.

01:06:16.580 --> 01:06:20.490
Yeah, he's good I call you a dumb head. You know, muscle is not the summing thing to be

01:06:20.490 --> 01:06:25.810
proud of. Gorillaz got bigger than anybody else. Maybe you learned to use your brain.

01:06:25.810 --> 01:06:29.800
Think, not hit. He's right to call you a dumb head, you.

01:06:30.700 --> 01:06:37.270
Weak, dress up all the time, clothes, the girls, everything but the bank.

01:06:38.010 --> 01:06:41.110
The bank, the bank of Gino Monetti, Gino Monetti and his sons.

01:06:41.790 --> 01:06:45.430
That's what I work and build for. That's why I live.

01:06:48.590 --> 01:06:55.330
But no more. I haven't no sons. I have strangers.

01:06:56.710 --> 01:06:57.390
Go on, get out.

01:07:22.460 --> 01:07:26.220
We'll beat it without them, Pa. You don't need them.

01:07:26.220 --> 01:07:28.770
You'd better get some sleep. We've got an awful lot to do tomorrow.

01:07:42.000 --> 01:07:45.170
Mama, why you don't talk to me no more?

01:07:46.330 --> 01:07:48.150
Why don't I hear you laughing no more?

01:07:48.450 --> 01:07:49.590
What happened to you?

01:07:50.780 --> 01:07:52.920
- Maybe I get old. - Old?

01:07:53.310 --> 01:07:55.640
Maybe a little grey, but not old.

01:07:56.120 --> 01:07:57.590
It's a pretty colour grey.

01:07:58.880 --> 01:08:00.000
We have plenty of good time again.

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:04.820
Soon Maxi fix everything and then you and me would take a little trip, huh?

01:08:04.820 --> 01:08:09.220
Palermo. You like to go back to Palermo once more, Mama?

01:08:09.220 --> 01:08:12.410
I wish we never leave all country, Gino.

01:08:12.410 --> 01:08:14.990
Oh, we have nothing there. Here we got everything.

01:08:14.990 --> 01:08:16.490
Here we got nothing.

01:08:16.490 --> 01:08:20.350
What do you mean? This is a fine house, a money, servants, a cars, a diamonds?

01:08:20.350 --> 01:08:21.350
You call it this nothing?

01:08:21.350 --> 01:08:25.910
We poor, Gino. When we only have Baba's shop, we rich.

01:08:25.910 --> 01:08:30.000
We love each other. The boys do.

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:35.070
You, me, now he's no more love.

01:08:36.220 --> 01:08:37.220
He's only hate.

01:08:45.680 --> 01:08:47.550
You said you were a barber.

01:08:47.770 --> 01:08:47.990
Say.

01:08:48.360 --> 01:08:49.300
How did you become a banker?

01:08:50.100 --> 01:08:50.760
I tell you.

01:08:51.250 --> 01:08:53.010
My wife, she's going to have a baby.

01:08:54.000 --> 01:08:56.170
My littlest son, Pietro.

01:08:57.020 --> 01:08:59.080
Why did the doctor say I needed $50 for the hospital?

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:01.960
I go to Giuseppe asking for $50.

01:09:01.960 --> 01:09:07.410
He make out the paper and say, "I gotta pay him back a $75."

01:09:07.410 --> 01:09:09.890
I say, "Is it too much?"

01:09:09.890 --> 01:09:12.010
You say, "All right, then go to bank."

01:09:12.010 --> 01:09:14.280
So I go to bank. They say, "I gotta have a collateral."

01:09:14.280 --> 01:09:17.650
So I say, "What is it, this collateral?"

01:09:17.650 --> 01:09:21.350
They tell him, "Is it something good, just like money?"

01:09:21.350 --> 01:09:25.120
So I say, "If I got a collateral, what for? I need money."

01:09:25.120 --> 01:09:26.840
And they say, "Goodbye."

01:09:26.840 --> 01:09:30.000
So I go back to Giuseppe, signed the paper.

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:32.860
Forget the money my wife had with the baby, everything okay.

01:09:33.860 --> 01:09:38.140
If your honor, please, what does all this talk about babies got to do with the banking act?

01:09:38.390 --> 01:09:39.770
What's the matter? You don't like babies?

01:09:41.200 --> 01:09:43.780
Court recessed until 1.30.

01:09:46.330 --> 01:09:58.080
My horse, she dies, so I go see my friend, Gina.

01:09:58.350 --> 01:09:59.670
How much money did he loan you?

01:10:00.060 --> 01:10:04.740
- He gave me $120. - And how much do you owe the bank now?

01:10:04.810 --> 01:10:09.510
He say, uh, uh, $287.33.

01:10:09.590 --> 01:10:11.910
$287.33.

01:10:12.410 --> 01:10:16.130
- Did you ever borrow more than the original $120? - No.

01:10:16.210 --> 01:10:19.330
Then what's the extra $167.33 for?

01:10:19.410 --> 01:10:22.550
Ah, there is interest combined, no?

01:10:22.630 --> 01:10:25.830
And a carrying charge and to record the note.

01:10:26.070 --> 01:10:29.730
- And I try to pay. - You never pay, not the one cent.

01:10:30.060 --> 01:10:33.060
How am I going to pay when I got no money? My new horse, she died too!

01:10:33.060 --> 01:10:37.060
What is it not my fault? You a horse killer! You promised to pay, you never pay!

01:10:37.060 --> 01:10:39.880
- You're a witness? - No questions.

01:10:39.880 --> 01:10:40.710
Step down.

01:10:53.230 --> 01:10:56.230
Most of your business was done with people from the east side, wasn't it?

01:10:56.230 --> 01:10:58.120
My bank is not on the Wall Street.

01:10:58.120 --> 01:11:00.000
Just answer the questions yes or no.

01:11:00.090 --> 01:11:04.110
- Yes. - People who live on the east side are mostly poor, aren't they?

01:11:04.210 --> 01:11:08.360
- Yes and no. - Depending on whether they lend money or borrow it.

01:11:08.960 --> 01:11:12.330
So you know how hard it is for these people just to make a living?

01:11:12.390 --> 01:11:16.050
- It's not easy. - Then how could you ever expect them to pay such interest?

01:11:16.130 --> 01:11:19.370
- Well, I wait until they have it. - Most of them never have it?

01:11:19.920 --> 01:11:22.110
How many homes have you foreclosed?

01:11:22.430 --> 01:11:24.340
How many salaries have you garnished?

01:11:24.700 --> 01:11:26.400
How many men have you sent into bankruptcy?

01:11:26.500 --> 01:11:28.300
I instruct the witness not to answer these questions.

01:11:28.400 --> 01:11:29.890
The facts are all in the bank records.

01:11:30.280 --> 01:11:31.940
Answer everything. I'm not afraid.

01:11:32.200 --> 01:11:34.080
The questions are improper. You don't have to answer them.

01:11:34.280 --> 01:11:36.880
Oh, let them ask. I tell. I got nothing to hide.

01:11:37.420 --> 01:11:40.220
You say you loan money on people, not collateral.

01:11:41.620 --> 01:11:45.880
When you foreclose on collateral, all you take away is a man's property.

01:11:46.800 --> 01:11:52.480
But when you garnish a man's wages, you take his sweat, his blood, the bread out of his children's mouths.

01:11:52.860 --> 01:11:55.490
You call that helping people? I call it usurious.

01:11:56.080 --> 01:12:00.000
I accuse you of being a lecherous moneylender, a disgrace to every detail.

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:02.000
You don't talk to Gino like that.

01:12:02.000 --> 01:12:04.850
- Nobody talk to Gino like that. - Shut up, Pop!

01:12:04.850 --> 01:12:06.850
You shut up! He's a free country.

01:12:06.850 --> 01:12:09.280
I do what I think is right, and what I think is right is right.

01:12:09.280 --> 01:12:11.450
I don't care what anybody say.

01:12:11.450 --> 01:12:13.450
Not to you, not to you, and not to you, mister.

01:12:13.450 --> 01:12:15.450
I'm Gino Manetti.

01:12:15.450 --> 01:12:17.450
No one telling me what to do.

01:12:17.450 --> 01:12:19.520
No one's telling me what to do.

01:12:32.170 --> 01:12:34.870
- Well, what do you think, Joe?

01:12:34.870 --> 01:12:36.170
- I'm no lawyer.

01:12:36.170 --> 01:12:38.550
I don't know what goes on in a jury's mind.

01:12:38.550 --> 01:12:39.390
- Who does?

01:12:39.390 --> 01:12:42.440
You don't have to be a lawyer to see it's going bad.

01:12:42.440 --> 01:12:44.430
- The old man's just asking for it.

01:12:44.430 --> 01:12:45.870
- You can't let them get back on the stand tomorrow.

01:12:45.870 --> 01:12:49.000
They're ripping to pieces.

01:12:49.000 --> 01:12:51.880
Why don't you sit there stuffing yourself?

01:12:51.880 --> 01:12:53.640
- What's the proper etiquette at a time like this?

01:12:53.640 --> 01:12:55.940
To stop beating?

01:12:55.940 --> 01:12:58.240
- I've got an idea, Joe.

01:12:58.240 --> 01:12:59.700
It's a long shot and it's dangerous.

01:13:01.020 --> 01:13:03.580
- I think we've got one of the jurors on our side.

01:13:03.580 --> 01:13:05.120
Once the other 11 start working on her,

01:13:05.120 --> 01:13:06.420
then she'll never hold out.

01:13:06.420 --> 01:13:07.780
- Yeah.

01:13:07.780 --> 01:13:10.060
- The idea is to see she does hold out.

01:13:10.060 --> 01:13:14.310
- Oh.

01:13:14.310 --> 01:13:17.550
- Somebody has to talk to her, tonight.

01:13:17.550 --> 01:13:20.580
- Is this the secret of Max Minetti's success?

01:13:20.580 --> 01:13:22.170
- You gotta sue her for her mind.

01:13:22.170 --> 01:13:24.170
Someday you're gonna fall in.

01:13:24.170 --> 01:13:26.740
- Meantime, I'll drink my beer.

01:13:26.740 --> 01:13:29.180
- Who's gonna talk to that juror?

01:13:29.180 --> 01:13:29.890
- Not me.

01:13:32.200 --> 01:13:36.230
- The other boys aren't smart enough. - One of them is. You.

01:13:36.230 --> 01:13:40.220
I thought of that. I may not be able to get near her.

01:13:40.220 --> 01:13:43.150
If she turns me down, the old man will really be nailed.

01:13:43.150 --> 01:13:50.760
You, she doesn't know. What do you say, Joe?

01:13:50.760 --> 01:13:53.520
I've said it many times. You want to hear it again?

01:13:53.520 --> 01:13:58.000
All right. If the old man got himself in, let him get himself out.

01:13:58.000 --> 01:13:59.760
This is the time I'll remember.

01:14:09.280 --> 01:14:29.460
lady friend finally showed up. She wants to see you. What's on your mind? Trial. I saw you. Sit down, Max. Please.

01:14:33.100 --> 01:14:36.640
- It's not going well, is it? - It's not over yet.

01:14:36.640 --> 01:14:41.400
- Where's your husband? - Danny. He's in Chicago.

01:14:41.400 --> 01:14:46.130
- Taking a big chance, isn't it? What if you get lonesome? - As a matter of fact, I am.

01:14:46.130 --> 01:14:51.640
- I don't handle that kind of work these days. - Danny and I aren't married.

01:14:51.640 --> 01:14:54.880
We had it out that same night. I didn't love him.

01:14:54.880 --> 01:15:00.000
I was just using him to cut out something that was hurting me. It was no use.

01:15:12.250 --> 01:15:16.460
That Minetti touch. If they'd only let you kiss the jury.

01:15:16.460 --> 01:15:20.580
Maybe I've got a call to make. I'll pick you up in an hour.

01:15:20.580 --> 01:15:23.790
I know about these night calls. Is it that important?

01:15:23.790 --> 01:15:25.000
Yes, it is.

01:15:25.000 --> 01:15:26.920
Not tonight. It can't be. Call it off.

01:15:26.920 --> 01:15:30.000
I can't. The party doesn't even know I'm coming.

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:31.920
- You know they'll be there.

01:15:31.920 --> 01:15:34.160
- I've got a feeling I'm expected.

01:15:34.160 --> 01:15:36.820
- They don't know you're coming yet you think you're expected.

01:15:36.820 --> 01:15:38.120
That's a strange date.

01:15:38.120 --> 01:15:41.030
- It's something new, even for me.

01:15:41.030 --> 01:15:42.210
- What's it about, Max?

01:15:42.210 --> 01:15:43.210
- Nothing to worry you.

01:15:43.210 --> 01:15:44.940
- I'll drive you and wait for you.

01:15:44.940 --> 01:15:46.080
- No, you don't want to sit in the car.

01:15:46.080 --> 01:15:47.340
I'll take a cab and be right over.

01:15:47.340 --> 01:15:52.370
- I'm driving you, period.

01:16:29.440 --> 01:16:30.000
May I come in?

01:16:37.740 --> 01:16:43.050
- Is anyone here? - The children, they're in bed.

01:16:43.050 --> 01:16:48.350
- You shouldn't be here. - There's lots of things shouldn't be.

01:16:48.350 --> 01:16:55.190
- If anyone found out. - Not much of a view, especially for kids.

01:16:55.190 --> 01:16:58.160
This is the best I can do since my husband died.

01:17:01.720 --> 01:17:02.740
I've never done this before.

01:17:03.920 --> 01:17:04.850
Do you believe me?

01:17:06.050 --> 01:17:06.560
Yes.

01:17:07.910 --> 01:17:10.490
Sending my father to jail isn't going to make this a better world.

01:17:12.100 --> 01:17:12.700
What are his chances?

01:17:14.000 --> 01:17:15.860
I can't tell you.

01:17:16.120 --> 01:17:16.920
You mean you don't want to?

01:17:17.440 --> 01:17:18.620
I'm under oath.

01:17:19.820 --> 01:17:22.110
You're a good woman, aren't you?

01:17:22.590 --> 01:17:23.700
I try to be.

01:17:24.280 --> 01:17:24.940
And a good mother.

01:17:25.840 --> 01:17:26.970
They're all I have.

01:17:29.350 --> 01:17:30.000
What do you make a week?

01:17:31.020 --> 01:17:39.350
- $32.50? - Who will it hurt?

01:17:42.290 --> 01:17:51.350
- I know you wouldn't do it for yourself. - Please go.

01:18:00.600 --> 01:18:09.560
- And take this with you. - Well, I tried.

01:18:09.560 --> 01:18:11.730
You must love your father a great deal.

01:18:11.730 --> 01:18:16.360
- I'm all he's got. - You'd better not stay alone now.

01:18:31.400 --> 01:18:32.530
I'm coming, darling.

01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:04.190
We can't have a whole thing if I do it in the whole thing.

01:20:04.190 --> 01:20:08.810
I'll talk about it later.

01:20:08.810 --> 01:20:11.010
Couldn't I tell you to stop coming here?

01:20:11.010 --> 01:20:12.130
I'm not in jail yet.

01:20:12.130 --> 01:20:13.130
I go what I please.

01:20:13.130 --> 01:20:14.630
Your new trial starts in a week.

01:20:14.630 --> 01:20:16.050
It isn't good for you to be seen here.

01:20:16.050 --> 01:20:17.010
This is a new bank.

01:20:17.010 --> 01:20:17.890
What do you mean it's a new bank?

01:20:17.890 --> 01:20:18.850
It's in my bank.

01:20:18.850 --> 01:20:20.130
Let's get that very clear.

01:20:20.130 --> 01:20:21.200
This isn't your bank.

01:20:21.200 --> 01:20:22.280
You don't own a nickel of it.

01:20:22.280 --> 01:20:23.360
You signed it over to Ma.

01:20:23.360 --> 01:20:24.820
Ma signed it over to us.

01:20:24.820 --> 01:20:26.060
Well, I only give it to Ma, so there'll

01:20:26.060 --> 01:20:27.780
be nothing in my name when the trial comes.

01:20:27.780 --> 01:20:29.280
She has no right to give it to you.

01:20:29.280 --> 01:20:30.000
We do things legal.

01:20:30.000 --> 01:20:35.140
Legally, she had the right. Legally, she signed it over to us, me, Tony, and Pietro.

01:20:35.140 --> 01:20:38.140
Well, you, Tony and Pietro, legally dirty crooks.

01:20:38.140 --> 01:20:42.220
He's my bank. The bank is mine. The money is mine. The name is mine.

01:20:42.220 --> 01:20:46.770
The name we hope to live down. In the meantime, you stay away from here.

01:20:46.770 --> 01:20:50.750
You can live in the big house with Ma. We'll pay all the bills.

01:20:50.750 --> 01:20:53.750
You get $40 a week for spending money. Learn to smoke cheaper cigars.

01:20:53.750 --> 01:20:56.800
And if you ever so much as set foot in this bank, you get nothing.

01:20:56.800 --> 01:20:59.060
What I do? Where I go?

01:21:00.030 --> 01:21:01.710
You're an old man. Buy peanuts.

01:21:02.230 --> 01:21:03.550
Go in the park, sit on the bench.

01:21:03.870 --> 01:21:05.010
Feed the peanuts to the pigeons.

01:21:09.640 --> 01:21:14.170
Crazy, get him out of here.

01:21:14.390 --> 01:21:15.190
You better go, Pop.

01:21:17.560 --> 01:21:20.330
You're going to be sorry, Joe.

01:21:20.720 --> 01:21:21.890
I promise you.

01:21:55.720 --> 01:21:57.890
What's happened to you, Pa? You don't look good.

01:21:58.610 --> 01:21:59.960
You don't look like a man who beat the rat.

01:22:00.160 --> 01:22:07.190
free man. What the good is it to be free? I got nothing to do. I got nowhere else to go. How's the

01:22:07.190 --> 01:22:12.340
new bank coming along? It's your brother's banker, not mine. It's in their name, that's all. Just a way

01:22:12.340 --> 01:22:17.670
of protecting the assets in case... No, it's a way to throw me out. You say I'm an old man, no good

01:22:17.670 --> 01:22:24.630
for nothing. Go sit in the park and tell me, feed the pigeons. Go away, old man. They steal the bank from me, Max.

01:22:25.350 --> 01:22:30.000
I like to sit in the park and feed the pigeons. You think? Feel the sun on my face, get up, walk around when I

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:32.920
Instead of you stuck in jail here like a rat in a trap, huh?

01:22:32.920 --> 01:22:35.800
Who put you here, Max?

01:22:35.800 --> 01:22:38.230
The sovereign state of New York.

01:22:38.230 --> 01:22:41.230
No, no, you brought a Joe. You brought a Joe, go call the police.

01:22:41.230 --> 01:22:44.560
You're mixed up, Pa. Even Joe wouldn't do a thing like that.

01:22:44.560 --> 01:22:47.560
When you go see the lady that night, don't know anything about it.

01:22:47.560 --> 01:22:51.570
You and Joe, nobody else, huh? When you come out, the police will wait for you.

01:22:51.570 --> 01:22:54.740
Who else but Joe? Look at what he'd do to me.

01:22:54.740 --> 01:22:59.250
Besides, someone tell me it was a Joe. Someone who'd hear him talk.

01:23:00.000 --> 01:23:11.690
- Who told you? - Maria asking me to give you this. She cried.

01:23:11.690 --> 01:23:17.590
- I expected it. - She gonna marry Tony. Tony is gonna be vice-president of the bank.

01:23:17.590 --> 01:23:21.590
- How about Pietro? - Oh, he's gonna be a second vice-president.

01:23:21.590 --> 01:23:25.600
- Not bad. - We don't let him do this to us, Max.

01:23:25.600 --> 01:23:30.000
Some day you get out. We take back the bank. Everything that they rob her from us.

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:31.000
You'll get it back, Maria.

01:23:31.000 --> 01:23:32.000
I don't want Maria.

01:23:32.000 --> 01:23:34.590
When I get out, I want to forget the whole thing.

01:23:34.590 --> 01:23:35.590
Oh, no, no, no, Max.

01:23:35.590 --> 01:23:36.590
You must not forget.

01:23:36.590 --> 01:23:37.590
You've got to make them pay.

01:23:37.590 --> 01:23:41.150
They steal it from me, what I work my whole life for.

01:23:41.150 --> 01:23:43.170
I work 16 hours a day, all kind of sweater shop.

01:23:43.170 --> 01:23:44.170
I save every penny.

01:23:44.170 --> 01:23:46.170
For years, I sweat in the barber shop.

01:23:46.170 --> 01:23:47.170
You remember?

01:23:47.170 --> 01:23:48.170
I do without everything.

01:23:48.170 --> 01:23:49.170
I wear one pair of shoes, one suit.

01:23:49.170 --> 01:23:50.170
I save it for years.

01:23:50.170 --> 01:23:51.170
For what?

01:23:51.170 --> 01:23:53.510
The bank.

01:23:53.510 --> 01:23:54.510
The bank is in my life.

01:23:54.510 --> 01:23:55.510
It's in my blood.

01:23:55.510 --> 01:23:58.000
They're killing me, Max.

01:23:58.000 --> 01:24:00.000
They take away me.

01:24:00.190 --> 01:24:03.830
blood. I can't live much more.

01:24:03.930 --> 01:24:05.370
I can't fight much more.

01:24:05.890 --> 01:24:07.510
I got nobody left. Only got you.

01:24:08.730 --> 01:24:09.990
You got to fix the max.

01:24:10.390 --> 01:24:12.700
For me. You got to do this for me.

01:24:13.180 --> 01:24:15.000
You got to make them pay.

01:24:16.680 --> 01:24:19.370
Forget about it, Pa.

01:24:20.780 --> 01:24:22.400
They'll pay.

01:24:31.180 --> 01:25:00.000
May I please see Mr. Manetti?

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:02.920
They open a new banker soon.

01:25:02.920 --> 01:25:04.900
Me they don't invite.

01:25:04.900 --> 01:25:08.070
They sent Pietro down to say I better keep away.

01:25:08.070 --> 01:25:09.930
I'm right of this to Max.

01:25:09.930 --> 01:25:11.100
Why?

01:25:11.100 --> 01:25:12.100
I tell Max everything.

01:25:12.100 --> 01:25:13.100
Why?

01:25:13.100 --> 01:25:16.250
Because of Max such things he's got to know.

01:25:16.250 --> 01:25:18.260
And what do you use on your pen?

01:25:18.260 --> 01:25:20.260
Just plain poison or some special kind?

01:25:20.260 --> 01:25:23.370
Isn't it bad enough for him locked up for years?

01:25:23.370 --> 01:25:25.370
Do you want to drive him crazy with your letters?

01:25:25.370 --> 01:25:27.540
You're Tony Pietro.

01:25:27.540 --> 01:25:29.470
Max hates them.

01:25:30.160 --> 01:25:31.560
- I want he should hate them.

01:25:31.560 --> 01:25:32.760
I want he should never stop.

01:25:32.760 --> 01:25:35.100
- You've never wanted anything else from any of them.

01:25:35.100 --> 01:25:39.340
Joe, Tony, Pietro, or Max.

01:25:39.340 --> 01:25:42.430
When you die, what a treasure you'll leave to the world.

01:25:42.430 --> 01:25:44.210
Four men full of hate.

01:25:44.210 --> 01:25:45.510
- These are my sons.

01:25:45.510 --> 01:25:46.570
This is none of your business.

01:25:46.570 --> 01:25:48.310
- One of them is, I love him.

01:25:48.310 --> 01:25:51.740
I want him to love me, to be able to love me.

01:25:51.740 --> 01:25:53.280
- This is none of your business.

01:25:53.280 --> 01:25:54.650
- Don't write that letter.

01:25:54.650 --> 01:25:56.990
Don't send anymore, leave him alone.

01:25:56.990 --> 01:25:58.600
Give him a chance.

01:25:58.600 --> 01:26:00.000
You've ruined his life up to now.

01:26:00.000 --> 01:26:01.340
Let him have it from now on.

01:26:01.340 --> 01:26:03.580
Stop filling him full of poison and hate.

01:26:03.580 --> 01:26:05.680
No, I don't want a Max a should forget.

01:26:05.680 --> 01:26:07.980
I write to me today, tomorrow, every day.

01:26:07.980 --> 01:26:09.560
I don't want a Max a should forget.

01:26:09.560 --> 01:26:11.320
Then he'll wind up hating you too,

01:26:11.320 --> 01:26:21.330
just like everyone else in the world hates you.

01:26:21.330 --> 01:26:22.450
Get out of my house.

01:26:22.450 --> 01:26:25.310
Tell Max about me.

01:26:25.310 --> 01:26:28.840
Tell Max his girl hates his father.

01:26:28.840 --> 01:26:30.000
Tell him his girl wishes

01:26:30.000 --> 01:26:32.530
and his father were rotting in jail instead.

01:26:32.530 --> 01:26:36.210
- Now get out! - You think of that sometimes, don't you?

01:26:36.280 --> 01:26:39.280
That you belong up there, instead of Max.

01:27:43.150 --> 01:27:44.390
Let's go.

01:27:44.390 --> 01:27:45.600
Where?

01:27:45.600 --> 01:27:47.090
Even with a 12-hour pass to see someone.

01:29:29.310 --> 01:29:30.000
Now, you make...

01:29:30.030 --> 01:29:32.810
Gino happy. Now you go back

01:29:32.810 --> 01:29:35.810
to jail happy. You stay up

01:29:35.810 --> 01:29:38.360
nights. You make all kinds

01:29:38.360 --> 01:29:40.180
of plans. Smart

01:29:40.180 --> 01:29:41.980
plans. You kill

01:29:41.980 --> 01:29:43.600
Joe. Joe kill you.

01:29:44.160 --> 01:29:45.500
Gino very happy.

01:29:48.940 --> 01:29:50.180
Once I have a husband,

01:29:50.800 --> 01:29:53.360
I give him four sons.

01:29:55.260 --> 01:29:56.370
Now I have nobody.

01:29:57.860 --> 01:29:58.540
No husband.

01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:00.760
Innocence.

01:30:02.510 --> 01:30:03.230
Go, Max.

01:30:04.390 --> 01:30:05.470
Go away.

01:30:07.300 --> 01:30:07.940
Fafia!

01:30:09.160 --> 01:30:10.330
Fafia!

01:31:37.390 --> 01:31:39.220
Well, Pa, where do we start?

01:31:39.470 --> 01:31:41.520
And Joe, Tony or Pietro?

01:31:41.660 --> 01:31:44.850
Can't waste time with Pietro, not a dumb head.

01:31:44.950 --> 01:31:47.810
That's what he is, isn't he, Pa? Isn't that what you always called him?

01:31:47.830 --> 01:31:53.140
Maybe Tony. I could take Marie away from him.

01:31:53.190 --> 01:31:54.260
That would break him up.

01:31:54.430 --> 01:31:56.750
Take his kid away, too. The kid always goes with the mother.

01:31:56.760 --> 01:32:00.000
And that would leave Tony with only his job at the bank.

01:32:00.410 --> 01:32:02.050
The bank comes next.

01:32:02.050 --> 01:32:04.170
A nice, big, juicy scandal.

01:32:04.170 --> 01:32:05.860
We'll start an investigation.

01:32:05.860 --> 01:32:08.420
Maybe even get an indictment with the grand jury.

01:32:08.420 --> 01:32:09.720
That'll take care of Joe.

01:32:09.720 --> 01:32:11.380
Elaine would leave him cold.

01:32:11.380 --> 01:32:15.190
With the bank gone, Pietro'll wind up a human punching bag.

01:32:15.190 --> 01:32:17.120
You'd like that, wouldn't you, Pa?

01:32:17.120 --> 01:32:19.080
That'll make your rest easy.

01:32:19.080 --> 01:32:22.340
You've always had it your way living, and you'd like it your way dead, too.

01:32:22.340 --> 01:32:23.300
Dog eat dog.

01:32:23.300 --> 01:32:24.750
Never forgive, never forget.

01:32:24.750 --> 01:32:28.480
You raised us that way, didn't you?

01:32:28.480 --> 01:32:29.860
Well, I got news for you, Pa.

01:32:30.760 --> 01:32:34.460
Tony can keep Maria. Joe can have his bank. Pietro can have his vice-presidency.

01:32:36.100 --> 01:32:40.140
I've got Irene. I lost seven years with her.

01:32:40.790 --> 01:32:43.980
They could have been seven wonderful years, and I threw them away.

01:32:44.700 --> 01:32:45.600
I buried them with you.

01:32:47.360 --> 01:32:49.080
But that's all you're getting, Pa. Not one more second.

01:32:49.930 --> 01:32:50.810
You've had all you're going to get.

01:32:51.600 --> 01:32:55.320
I've come back to life, Pa.

01:33:48.810 --> 01:33:51.110
Hello, baby. Max. We can still make that plane.

01:33:51.890 --> 01:33:53.110
Come and get me. I'm at the old house.

01:33:57.060 --> 01:33:58.200
What's the matter? Can't you hear me?

01:34:01.400 --> 01:34:05.760
- Say something. - Oh, Max! Max!

01:34:05.760 --> 01:34:08.770
- I'm coming as fast as I can. - Well, make it faster, period.

01:34:08.770 --> 01:34:21.920
Welcome home, brothers. I'm glad you've come.

01:34:21.920 --> 01:34:25.200
I've got news for you, good news. It calls for a celebration.

01:34:25.200 --> 01:34:27.440
Pietro, you know where the wine is. Get it out.

01:34:27.440 --> 01:34:30.000
We'll all have one last drink together.

01:34:30.120 --> 01:34:32.360
- In brotherly love.

01:34:32.360 --> 01:34:39.880
It's a pity pie isn't here to see it.

01:34:39.880 --> 01:34:44.050
- What's the matter?

01:34:44.050 --> 01:34:45.130
- Only this morning you were falling

01:34:45.130 --> 01:34:46.960
all over one another to drink with me.

01:34:46.960 --> 01:34:50.230
- You gave us a bad time this morning, Max.

01:34:50.230 --> 01:34:52.130
My stomach's been upset all day.

01:34:52.130 --> 01:34:54.100
- You need a new diet, Joe.

01:34:54.100 --> 01:34:57.210
Look at me, hard as a rock, seven years, no pastries.

01:34:57.210 --> 01:34:58.030
That's what does it.

01:34:58.030 --> 01:34:59.380
- I like to sleep nights.

01:35:00.440 --> 01:35:04.130
I don't want to go to bed worrying about my kids, my home, the bank.

01:35:04.590 --> 01:35:06.430
Life isn't worthwhile if you've got to worry.

01:35:06.510 --> 01:35:08.370
Well, if you're worried about me, you can stop.

01:35:08.610 --> 01:35:10.950
Once I step out of this house, you'll never see me again.

01:35:11.250 --> 01:35:13.010
A change of heart, is that it?

01:35:13.130 --> 01:35:14.350
Change of mind.

01:35:14.460 --> 01:35:16.440
All of a sudden, you're a new man.

01:35:16.950 --> 01:35:19.900
The vendetta's off, just like that.

01:35:21.110 --> 01:35:22.950
Who do you think you're talking to?

01:35:23.590 --> 01:35:25.370
You're no different than the old man.

01:35:25.450 --> 01:35:26.870
Pa never changed, neither will you.

01:35:26.950 --> 01:35:28.800
You've both got the same blood.

01:35:29.350 --> 01:35:30.000
Well, so have I.

01:35:30.000 --> 01:35:32.530
That's one thing you forgot.

01:35:32.530 --> 01:35:36.440
I've got an appointment. You're in my way.

01:35:36.440 --> 01:35:39.440
Pietro!

01:37:12.320 --> 01:37:16.650
That's because you've been in jail. You think you're tough.

01:37:16.650 --> 01:37:19.640
'Cause I sit in a bank all day, you think I'm soft.

01:37:19.640 --> 01:37:23.820
You're both born on Mulberry Street. I can be tough, too.

01:37:23.820 --> 01:37:26.330
One thing the old man taught me:

01:37:26.330 --> 01:37:29.730
Never give a guy a chance. When you've got him down, don't press your luck. Finish him.

01:37:30.540 --> 01:37:32.540
You don't have to fight the same guy twice.

01:37:32.540 --> 01:37:35.280
In some ways, the old man was right.

01:37:35.280 --> 01:37:58.100
Just leave it.

01:38:00.000 --> 01:38:27.840
Don't you want to keep your job in the bank? You want to live bring him up bring him out. Yes, throw him over

01:38:30.000 --> 01:38:31.260
Sit over, dumb head.

01:38:33.040 --> 01:38:34.330
Dumb head.

01:38:34.700 --> 01:38:35.260
Dumb head.

01:38:35.640 --> 01:38:36.180
Dumb head.

01:38:36.520 --> 01:38:37.060
Dumb head.

01:39:01.150 --> 01:39:05.960
- That's right, don't do it, it's Pa driving.

01:39:05.960 --> 01:39:08.180
Pa wants you to kill Joe.

01:39:08.180 --> 01:39:10.350
You're not a dumb head, be smart.

01:39:10.350 --> 01:39:12.520
If you kill Joe, you kill him for Pa.
